freedreno: skip draws with NULL BOs after GPU OOM (OnePlus 6 / SweetGPU)

With a 32 MiB SweetGPU carve-out, once GPU memory is exhausted,
fd_resource_create() / realloc_bo() fails and leaves resources with
rsc->bo == NULL (or sub-allocations like bindless descriptor sets / LRZ
buffers fail to allocate a BO). Subsequent draws or clears that bind
those resources dereference rsc->bo or pass NULL to fd_bo_mark_for_dump /
fd_bo_ref, crashing backboardd.

- freedreno_draw.c / freedreno_draw.h: add fd_oom_note_skip() (logs once
  via mesa_loge and sweet_drm_log on __APPLE__, and counts skips) and
  helper checks for NULL BOs on bound vertex/index/SO/indirect buffers,
  shader UBOs/SSBOs/images/sampler views, and framebuffer surfaces.
  Skip fd_draw_vbo(), fd_clear(), fd_clear_render_target(),
  fd_clear_depth_stencil(), and fd_launch_grid() when any bound
  resource has rsc->bo == NULL.
- freedreno_blitter.c: skip fd_blit() and fd_resource_copy_region() when
  src or dst resource has rsc->bo == NULL.
- a6xx/fd6_image.cc: in fd6_build_bindless_state(), return NULL if
  fd_bo_new() or fd_bo_map() fails instead of calling
  fd_bo_mark_for_dump(NULL).
- a6xx/fd6_draw.cc: in fd6_clear(), guard subpass->lrz == NULL before
  calling fd_bo_ref().

Applies after 0001-0004. Mesa is MIT licensed; this patch is too.

